      "evidence": "template/scripts/finish_task.py: `except (OSError, SystemExit) as exc` in cleanup_earlier_tasks. cleanup_earlier_deferred in template/scripts/worktree_cleanup.py can raise other exceptions: `DeferredCleanupTarget.from_entry(entry)` on a malformed record, `commands[error[\"path\"]]` (KeyError if an error path differs from the entry path), and git subprocess errors. The spec says: \"a failure of this cleanup is a warning and does not change the delivery result\". The call also runs after the merge and after closure, so an unexpected exception there makes a successful delivery look failed.",
      "id": "earlier-cleanup-warning-catch-too-narrow",
      "severity": "advisory",
      "summary": "cleanup_earlier_tasks promises that any failure of earlier-task cleanup is only a warning. It catches only OSError and SystemExit, so other errors still turn a delivered finish into a traceback and non-zero exit."
